.TH STRALLOC_CASE_DIFFS 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
stralloc_case_diffs \- Compare a stralloc with a string, ignoring case

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>
.IB #include <lib/str.h>
.IB #include <lib/stralloc.h>

.IB int
.IB stralloc_case_diffs(const stralloc* sa, const char* s);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBstralloc_case_diffs\fR function compares a stralloc \fIsa\fR with a string \fIs\fR, ignoring case differences, and returns the result of the comparison.

.SH PARAMETERS
.IB sa
The stralloc to compare.

.IB s
The string to compare.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fBstralloc_case_diffs\fR function returns 0 if the stralloc and the string are equal, a negative value if \fIsa\fR is less than \fIs\fR, and a positive value if \fIsa\fR is greater than \fIs\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBstralloc_case_diffs\fR function to compare a stralloc with a string:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/byte.h>
#include <lib/str.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>

int main() {
    stralloc sa;
    const char* s;

    stralloc_init(&sa);
    s = "example";

    // Your code to initialize sa here

    int result = stralloc_case_diffs(&sa, s);

    if (result == 0) {
        printf("stralloc and string are equal\n");
    } else if (result < 0) {
        printf("sa is less than s\n");
    } else {
        printf("sa is greater than s\n");
    }

    stralloc_done(&sa);

    return 0;
}
.nef